Z||000000||Austin||09-24-2001||02:56 PM||||I want some power seats for my Fiero.  I know that Trans Am seats will go in a Fiero and they can come with a power option.  But is it possible to use Power Trans Am seats tracks and put Fiero seats on them and put them in a Fiero.  If so has anybody done this before?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-24-2001||08:06 PM||||Sure you can, but you'll lose about 2" of headroom and 2" of legroom.  To be perfectly honest, why would you need any power adjustments (other than lumbar, thigh adjustment or bolster adjustment)?  You can't recline the seat (much).  Once you get it in position (front to back), you really don't need to move it much.  Personally, I'd keep the extra leg and headroom.||||reg||1
